      "side": "Russian",
      "summary": "The larger of Steinheil's two divisions, which had pushed south from Riga along the Aa. Attacked at Mesoten on the 29th, it fought hard along the river before falling back, and was driven on over the following days.",
      "notes": [
        "The division's own 2nd Jäger is attached to the Petrovsk regiment, as the list takes a Jäger regiment; its other Jäger regiment, the 44th, was detached on Åland.",
        "Battalion counts aren't certain: one account gives these regiments three battalions, the order of battle none. Two field battalions each are shown, the usual for 1812.",
        "Riehn gives the division '9,000 infantry, only 200 cavalry and twelve guns' at Mesoten, so the Finland Dragoons (three squadrons) are Small.",
